#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b4b32f9-8362-5c81-a1fe-4457d91ae571" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Functions That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "417b034a-4a1b-57ea-ae71-c3692dd9c074" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462169} {:answer/id #uuid "366f4957-2ec0-53a1-aaec-db78bf39c189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "366f4957-2ec0-53a1-aaec-db78bf39c189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462170} :answer-field/id #uuid "b33e6574-4ffa-5b8b-8bd3-5160e7158367" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462838} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2848015f-fd1c-524b-9770-6641ede3f19e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462171} {:answer/id #uuid "505d7bac-6415-5832-a400-b6da7b039903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2848015f-fd1c-524b-9770-6641ede3f19e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462171} :answer-field/id #uuid "9753bc53-75e5-5715-a073-5b1b466537bd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eee75ead-b5ed-510b-a4c5-d9a5d1757af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462173} {:answer/id #uuid "7796dc8d-ca52-55f7-aa70-af05b82e9eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7796dc8d-ca52-55f7-aa70-af05b82e9eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462174} :answer-field/id #uuid "629cf843-1a02-5f46-991b-cdafd055537c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "79dcb2e6-ddac-560d-acd7-0aceed9cb202" :question/math-academy-id "q-125259" :question/problem "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1]?$\n- **I.** $f(x)={e}^{x}$\n- **II.** $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|$\n- **III.** $h(x)=x|x|$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1],$ the function must be continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)={e}^{x}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1).$ Therefore, $f(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|$ is not defined at $x=0.$ Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $h(x)=x|x|$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it is continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only functions I and III satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f30993e-b5c7-5d8a-9b27-2aed2c9223e1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Sign of a Circulation From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb212b19-0efe-5595-8a6e-e47cc9adaa5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462175} {:answer/id #uuid "3d6f84f1-683f-5d00-9604-34d4790cb9c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb212b19-0efe-5595-8a6e-e47cc9adaa5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462175} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a39db3-475c-5e0a-801d-11e7e55a57ab" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ffe3f7d-d217-5537-9b72-5552de904647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462177} {:answer/id #uuid "0df6588a-1243-5256-a273-81f127138027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0df6588a-1243-5256-a273-81f127138027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462178} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b8dffca-0ed9-5da1-995f-1364b3fbea05" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32ca2cc7-24f7-507a-9285-aa88fa019e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462179} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea2a08c-0d10-592a-9aa9-d6c47c1f74d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32ca2cc7-24f7-507a-9285-aa88fa019e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462179} :answer-field/id #uuid "68723449-ccac-55e8-b16a-59ae779fc661" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4fa44014-b4ce-590d-a5cb-5c0b5e464aaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-125392" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dca985dc352c45477dbb6ada86ad5a9cfa4404969510191a1955e59b082709fe.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves around $C,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/eb/eb4da8143700c7d31e0ceacd09ac76a8d1bcb10379a34dce5b59d48f2ae58c13.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ remains unchanged.\n\n![](images/70/70a473397216589350f63482ab3e36cb1247e7825046c70642254c8514564b00.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dab6bfb9-608d-5ff8-88e7-5aa9612acda4" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a312728-759b-5a18-bc9a-7a468e2c468e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462181} {:answer/id #uuid "b006ccd8-dbf9-52a5-8de6-8656396b4437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a312728-759b-5a18-bc9a-7a468e2c468e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462181} :answer-field/id #uuid "c09c4b26-8176-500e-9d72-7fa8141a088c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "822889f3-1878-5472-943f-bc21421aa019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462183} {:answer/id #uuid "3f2cd909-af16-5666-9ee5-08e066d042c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f2cd909-af16-5666-9ee5-08e066d042c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462184} :answer-field/id #uuid "e45bb2d9-7504-598f-8971-17193667fabf" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c27fd31-ee21-5aab-a03c-e98f38a45ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462185} {:answer/id #uuid "e661237d-bcf6-5e01-b2dc-8992ab58d984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e661237d-bcf6-5e01-b2dc-8992ab58d984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462186} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebc3f15f-2730-55a5-bdbe-6cc6317a24d4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a58b62d-04d0-5a47-b1b2-408fc180c352" :question/math-academy-id "q-125487" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9da7dc42ad4e9eb5b6df7c42f06d7a0f7767820693f8e99e073c7b8bd7e93441.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/14/14e94a2c5d0faabff1beeadeccb6999aa2edd71fce06fff8a2655db74e585eba.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/c5/c54487081f2150216b7e41b1351f0f7b19c794b140297789f19d9afe830bd7b1.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dab6bfb9-608d-5ff8-88e7-5aa9612acda4" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d53d1d6-b5c4-5b67-bf25-7d27d099f803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462187} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea8a4ee-7a15-5906-a035-85b03d8a5bf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d53d1d6-b5c4-5b67-bf25-7d27d099f803" :an