r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/78/78de6ce0133bec33c14eabb43db2e53eb8d76653aa1fc121c83f47c4b91c3b94.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "831cb1b1-064e-559a-8090-c5ef5904d2b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463482} {:answer/id #uuid "f119cf42-93c5-5b60-9a16-92306e80bd8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "831cb1b1-064e-559a-8090-c5ef5904d2b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463482} :answer-field/id #uuid "069a4e64-f502-58b7-afe8-73851d7f80b9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464675} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a59c28f9-7a4d-56a4-8b36-20c269b2a473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463484} {:answer/id #uuid "984ca6d5-aa97-5d84-8ae3-06c8f43e8370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "984ca6d5-aa97-5d84-8ae3-06c8f43e8370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463485} :answer-field/id #uuid "5285b4f0-a29a-5753-9eed-ad304e29d4c6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464676} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3250d354-20d6-54d0-97fb-d9ecc4f3e804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463486} {:answer/id #uuid "e358fd30-0443-5b9f-be75-140d1a5f4544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e358fd30-0443-5b9f-be75-140d1a5f4544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463487} :answer-field/id #uuid "c43a9049-f742-5536-9ca5-222ebee9078f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91c88aa7-9c4e-5dd7-9c30-608f94c03554" :question/math-academy-id "q-125507" :question/problem "![](images/86/866a1812bd31e0443becf35a7cc2b8df1bc84a49091a94250b60fe3533e4b172.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semiellipse is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/e4/e4232577b0687d781f702a196ae2c0060d3264c1f44a45a404a0f9da03bc0dd1.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/f7/f7cfcef37ed6a52d5bd374fae2d7a00c4d8012e9ea8dbef43165c10bcc9471be.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f30993e-b5c7-5d8a-9b27-2aed2c9223e1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Sign of a Circulation From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a074685c-6f81-5431-86de-5f20c4658e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463488} {:answer/id #uuid "24e36323-76da-51e5-bfb2-592610002fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24e36323-76da-51e5-bfb2-592610002fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463489} :answer-field/id #uuid "c743c6e7-059d-5909-9335-e5ad04088599" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464678} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6209e29c-6f4f-5cd2-b854-a9a719c264fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463490} {:answer/id #uuid "a906d4ee-e6aa-54de-9527-ace41765eb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a906d4ee-e6aa-54de-9527-ace41765eb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463491} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fdabed2-ee70-5863-b4f7-2f54d7e967e7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13acff26-2b2e-5369-9c05-1a4ae2971db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463492} {:answer/id #uuid "21155136-2b73-54fb-aa55-8041c9107e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13acff26-2b2e-5369-9c05-1a4ae2971db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463492} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d92b4b5-1cec-55de-8dcb-2ff6ec78d476" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "547c79d0-6e8c-5db1-9245-a09abf6b78b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-125637" :question/problem "![](images/e6/e60f7c0adc3e2ec8daa3203564c31bf660e6eca7e6394955cc73133ac3673ed5.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/a8/a8010db8481768cb61d0734dcfc97eed646441ab265c4928d06d274ef0e1c1dd.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves **clockwise** along $C.$\n\n![](images/be/be263d706bfc3ef205be37aaed85d4984d3739d53cdaadb8cba88e3d5196ce93.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259835 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f30993e-b5c7-5d8a-9b27-2aed2c9223e1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Sign of a Circulation From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9988e87b-8bb7-5f6a-8c19-1f86b1e3bec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463494} {:answer/id #uuid "ead72610-955b-5f0a-a542-876b5f86cecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :