ld/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "982dcf8b-4c96-5db9-9ec4-1bcce43696b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-125643" :question/problem "![](images/f4/f4042d4eb43310480f3c75673befbf58067a89704d20b9a63f0f6c7272179f3e.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/fa/fabbbb78d8fd4d327fe82d1d93d8e0fc15dd33e909266e0ef88de931be28b951.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement I is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves **clockwise** along $C.$\n\n![](images/71/712564e3b0ad0e23d2d9097eb02c0857130bdaa6619a005738205130ab66ac3a.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567" :knowledge-point/title "Circulation in Conservative Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d433da7b-1e1e-535b-9f25-83bdf23e4df0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463500} {:answer/id #uuid "b9260be8-c900-5ecd-a29b-b1b5e76ddea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9260be8-c900-5ecd-a29b-b1b5e76ddea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463501} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f88a2a7-6b38-5992-98ee-3c8c44386624" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464684} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbb4515b-adce-511f-9f3e-7963532589f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463502} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0d50d9-8f3d-5d9f-b4f7-523d73146916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbb4515b-adce-511f-9f3e-7963532589f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463502} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7d2d666-5099-5d29-a783-b3acfcfc73d6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79a18ac3-3da5-5858-a2ae-9bb8d620bf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463504} {:answer/id #uuid "df41bbfc-30d2-5909-8569-78bc4270e186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79a18ac3-3da5-5858-a2ae-9bb8d620bf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463504} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6879713-fe19-5bab-b30b-1608ccbd903c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30840479-d77d-5e50-bc98-88470d99f8d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-125650" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)=x{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+y.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $∇f$ is conservative\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- **III.** ${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for some closed paths $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement II is false. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\n- Statement III is false. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567" :knowledge-point/title "