t} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2573021-ba50-5806-b30b-c6a0c1437efc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463579} :answer-field/id #uuid "42a586b0-b4ae-5007-897d-4fdfaee7b7bc" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "474bf73b-e366-5189-9675-bc39c5723be5" :question/math-academy-id "q-126204" :question/problem "Which of the following are zero matrices?\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $R$ is a zero matrix since *all* its entries are zeros.\n\n- $S$ is a zero matrix since *all* its entries are zeros.\n\n- $T$ is a zero matrix since *all* its entries are zeros.\n\nTherefore, $R$, $S$, and $T$ are zero matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13445-0218-5950-967e-a68bcfec32c7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe5658b2-ecbf-5729-a03d-3906b20cccbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463580} {:answer/id #uuid "21c517ff-d927-5410-8a65-4207f1706ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21c517ff-d927-5410-8a65-4207f1706ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463581} :answer-field/id #uuid "e80c3713-3550-5c60-bf0c-0821c17d963c" :answer-field/key "K" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7f323ab-c5d9-5fff-aecb-db53cbab4e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463582} {:answer/id #uuid "1560c66f-7a1a-5947-9f60-03688b1f8b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7f323ab-c5d9-5fff-aecb-db53cbab4e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463582} :answer-field/id #uuid "7be7bbda-907a-5513-a354-940218369f61" :answer-field/key "L" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3730365-1faa-567b-9c31-4acdc410ed4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463584} {:answer/id #uuid "869dcee3-6d63-5587-84d7-2a86bd969317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3730365-1faa-567b-9c31-4acdc410ed4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463584} :answer-field/id #uuid "3622dfcc-ed36-50f5-8709-40aff4162d7a" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0dc57098-3c69-5567-91db-1d90d4ec9c40" :question/math-academy-id "q-126275" :question/problem "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,L=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,M=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- $K$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $2$ rows and $2$ columns, so it is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- $L$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $1$ rows and $2$ columns, so it's a $1\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- $M$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $4$ rows and $3$ columns, so it's a $4\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, only $K$ is a square matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b4b32f9-8362-5c81-a1fe-4457d91ae571" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Functions That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3712d163-9e49-58ba-8e1d-eedad9bf9dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463586} {:answer/id #uuid "d7f5288f-ae92-5922-b531-3b721c1ad84c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3712d163-9e49-58ba-8e1d-eedad9bf9dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463586} :answer-field/id #uuid "99224ad4-ae6f-5c27-8559-5a850b63d8e3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464727} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68e18986-22e0-5c9e-9ee9-51a2e38aff6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463588} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd3c05f-0a49-5102-8ed1-cce210ce03cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cd3c05f-0a49-5102-8ed1-cce210ce03cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463589} :answer-field/id #uuid "55e8673f-1711-58a6-a4ca-27f64f2c9bd4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464728} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "432628a2-c729-5b1b-af1c-4fab9151d6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463590} {:answer/id #uuid "6ee48f3c-d665-5d30-840a-4fbe144185d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ee48f3c-d665-5d30-840a-4fbe144185d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463591} :answer-field/id #uuid "94fe4378-3ad5-5b97-be35-e7cc0517e7e4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "22f3b282-003f-570b-9433-d53609b5be7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127013" :question/problem "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1]?$\n\nI. $f(x)=2|x|$\n\nII. $g(x)=|x-1|$\n\nIII. $h(x)=|x+1|$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1],$ the function must be continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)=2|x|$ is continuous on $[-1,1],$ but it has a corner in $x=0.$ Hence, it is not differentiable at $x=0,$ which means it is not differentiable on $(-1,1).$ Therefore, $f(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $g(x)=|x-1|$ is continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1)$ because it is equivalent to $p(x)=1-x$ over the given interval. Therefore, $g(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem. Note that the graph of $y=g(x)$ has a corner point at $x=1$ but this point does not lie inside $(-1,1).$\n\n- The function $h(x)=|x+1|$ is continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1)$ because it is equivalent to $p(x)=x+1$ over the given interval. Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem. Note that the graph of $y=h(x)$ has a corner point at $x=-1$ but this point does not lie inside $(-1,1).$\n\nTherefore, only functions II and III satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262686 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b4b32f9-8362-5c81-a1fe-4457d91ae571" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Functions That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8424311-5774-5664-af5d-dfb6a6dc0336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463592} {:answer/id #uuid "e73779e5-1d0f-59d8-a3a1-18ac78c7b845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e73779e5-1d0f-59d