} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463614} {:answer/id #uuid "10df1e34-71fc-5eaf-b9c8-3da308db6b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46fa00f6-11fc-5e06-be3e-f6dba2027667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463614} :answer-field/id #uuid "8632d559-2742-5101-9099-c7c7ae2c0458" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "92477238-fcf4-57c0-a788-d4cbd2b1a3bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-127030" :question/problem "![](images/65/6504ab3dde96670102e5046887707416495895dc3b85a514b5bbe7b526b4fa42.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n- The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is zero\n- The flux of $F$ across $C$ is positive\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nTo understand the flux intuitively, we imagine that $F$ represents a stream of flowing water. The flux of $F$ across $C$ represents the net flow of water escaping the region bounded by $C:$ \n\n- If more water flows out through $C$ than in through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *out* through $C$), the flux is *positive*.\n\n- If more water flows in through $C$ than out through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *in* through $C$), the flux is *negative*.\n\n![](images/a7/a72dc9866562a42a49590fd169424307675b2c14b36833bd729026f46b677eec.png)\n\n- If the net flow through $C$ is zero then the flux equals zero.\n\n![](images/3a/3a6ac8656b2e0b5cc482a16eb3a4fab57cb681c9a40cf634da47f9a4323d9fdf.png)\n\nFor an arbitrary closed curve, the outward-pointing unit normal vector tells us which direction is \"out.\"\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement III is false. Note that the flux $F$ that flows in through $C$ is the same that flows out through $C.$ Therefore, there is no net flow of $F$ through $C.$\n\n![](images/9a/9af12f28947e46810074574dad9f6b9a8b572f116456807bf9c478d12da19ec2.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. When measuring flux through a closed curve, the orientation of the curve does not matter because the outward-pointing unit normal vector is the same at each point on $C$ in either case.\n\n![](images/c4/c4402595afc4ce12937794f0755a446ae738d3b47d7e9f4978b6344f9ef8909a.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $-C$ is zero, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{-C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b7b8782-d1f4-5654-a18f-6ad35de8fb30" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Flux's Sign From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "596e2f25-6344-5eef-8a75-204c85175502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463616} {:answer/id #uuid "f2be65cc-9a49-5f0b-8eef-59b759de229f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "596e2f25-6344-5eef-8a75-204c85175502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463616} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7d9b2de-be53-5786-80d4-7cae45fb50a3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464742} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "497c22f7-4edc-50c1-acb2-19f74b2baca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463618} {:answer/id #uuid "e235a714-1f0d-523a-8c12-6f930cfc72c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e235a714-1f0d-523a-8c12-6f930cfc72c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463619} :answer-field/id #uuid "45cc04e2-3594-5873-8ddb-dade30e36c6f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464743} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce71fa89-a63c-5932-a85a-15e6f162c9e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463620} {:answer/id #uuid "7ffa6d1d-e27b-5ef6-bf18-d9dcd01130db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ffa6d1d-e27b-5ef6-bf18-d9dcd01130db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463621} :answer-field/id #uuid "78427e4a-7c4c-55d1-bdbd-e9b61519ab8b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6542e3fc-27ed-5a91-abb0-bbb5f848f669" :question/math-academy-id "q-127032" :question/problem "![](images/45/453633f6309b9f1d2a3f7a8d4266ff10f571823cffd705d0bc93b930dce63d8f.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The flux of $F$ across $C$ is negative\n- The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n- The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is zero\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nTo understand the flux intuitively, we imagine that $F$ represents a stream of flowing water. The flux of $F$ across $C$ represents the net flow of water escaping the region bounded by $C:$ \n\n- If more water flows out through $C$ than in through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *out* through $C$), the flux is *positive*.\n\n- If more water flows in through $C$ than out through $C$ (i.e., there is a net flow *in* through $C$), the flux is *negative*.\n\n![](images/a7/a72dc9866562a42a49590fd169424307675b2c14b36833bd729026f46b677eec.png)\n\n- If the net flow through $C$ is zero then the flux equals zero.\n\n![](images/3a/3a6ac8656b2e0b5cc482a16eb3a4fab57cb681c9a40cf634da47f9a4323d9fdf.png)\n\nFor an arbitrary closed curve, the outward-pointing unit normal vector tells us which direction is \"out.\"\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. From the diagram below we see that $F$ acts perpendicular to $n$ at every point on $C.$ Therefore, there is no net flow of $F$ through $C.$\n\n![](images/84/844d5e5574571ae221a86f541820a4b215766451031f4eea678cee46a1b83e41.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. When measuring flux through a closed curve, the orientation of the curve does not matter because the outward-pointing unit normal vector is the same at each point on $C$ in either case.\n\n![](images/b8/b8b31d46646db2d88d8a3f5658ee876383795ad5ba9aa55eb9959d5f95c02dbe.png)\n\nSo, the flux of $F$ across $-C$ is zero, and we must have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{-C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175902 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "205c5518-c67a-5784-8cc7-55b42ce7fb0e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether the Extreme Value Theorem Is Applicable to a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf0d74d1-c4ec-5acb-8d02-428a673c8e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463622} {:answer/id #uuid "b27ccb3b-3a36-5770-a2e0-e34e1a22fdf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf0d74d1-c4ec-5acb-8d02-428a673c8e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463622} :answer-field/id #uuid "a80361de-cad8-5430-99d8-5688274c0393" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cabcedb4-c1ca-5e1a-b3ec-c2005b0b28e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463624} {:answer/id #uuid "b650e945-f362-5475-974d-8d17e8587aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cabcedb4-c1ca-5e1a-b3ec-c2005b0b28e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463624} :answer-field/id #uuid "d05e1564-e6cd-5fbc-8747-2e5f9ac1ae55" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464746} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "739b0c21-210c-5378-b8ae-1ebb085b817a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463626} {:answer/id #uuid "aacfd434-b805-551c-b330-1937375ff4cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aacfd434-b805-551c-b330-1937375ff4cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463627} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fbf5f4e-65f1-5792-8d50-6e668eb928a9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82be4976-c19d-544a-b202-bf6dca5175c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-127037" :question/problem "![](images/e9/e97552a634b4e3ad3604de9d75742af05aa30a18ee92c8440e6c3cedd5d7273a.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. On which of the following intervals is the extreme value theorem applicable to $f(x)?$\n\n- $[-4,-1]$\n- $[0,4]$\n- $[1,6]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-4,-1]$ is closed, but the function has a removable discontinuity at $x=-2.$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,4]$ is closed, but the function is not defined at $x=0.$ So, it can't be continuous at this point. Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[1,6]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[1,6].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175902 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "205c5518-c67a-5784-8cc7-55b42ce7fb0e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether the Extreme Value Theorem Is Applicable to a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8239025-1548-543f-b742-41d95cf7deb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463628} {:answer/id #uuid "9a82f1b3-42a5-578c-8649-06dea016a079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a82f1b3-42a5-578c-8649-06dea016a079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463629} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac1b256f-898f-56e9-b3f9-a86a572d532c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9c82c83-bf9b-5c1c-a3ac-23c8a77066be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463630} {:answer/id #uuid "95d01e78-945c-57a4-beeb-ad3daff03013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9c82c83-bf9b-5c1c-a3ac-23c8a77066be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463630} :answer-field/id #uuid "95ebfab1-477a-5fc2-8ce7-ed02f4886a9e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464749} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3cb2411-872b-5c5b-bca9-ffa9f1dfeca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463632} {:answer/id #uuid "76790a97-7368-5733-9ed1-932cc5f558e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3cb2411-872b-5c5b-bca9-ffa9f1dfeca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463632} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc644c42-a158-5323-b8b4-dd62841c3890" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "144d9fbc-7660-5ed9-9ae4-01d5a04d6a5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127040" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3c25115cfb7ccde7ec0cbec249d62b037c7fb94be92905b186101ce1fd45a1d8.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. On which interval is the extreme value theorem applicable to $f(x)?$\n\nI. $[0,2]$\n\nII. $(1,2)$\n\nIII. $(-\\infty ,0]$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[0,2]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[0,2].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(1,2)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $(-\\infty ,0]$ is closed, but it is not a bounded interval in the form $[a,b].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83031cf0-e568-5359-b7ee-f956035ef639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463634} {:answer/id #uuid "e4cf2a4d-34df-5aca-961e-fc888997d1ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4cf2a4d-34df-5aca-961e-fc888997d1ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463635} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdcbe749-383a-5cb7-9f78-d6159757abf9" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbb3d7ee-532c-5b06-b40b-f4c2dbe2d0d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463636} {:answer/id #uuid "eea6cd9f-fca7-5155-b38b-3664f40c5e11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbb3d7ee-532c-5b06-b40b-f4c2dbe2d0d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463636} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5a898ab-fc64-534b-9fa2-a231d2f0b959" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464752} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "367796bf-a0ff-5cf6-9aaf-31902587b686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463638} {:answer/id #uuid "0144a740-b964-5dd0-8cb7-ff3f206d1152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "367796bf-a0ff-5cf6-9aaf-31902587b686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463638} :answer-field/id #uuid "773e2d3e-4596-5ce9-b52a-b7bceb4276e2" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9987fa7a-d96a-5001-a5b8-b5e558e85078" :question/math-academy-id "q-127751" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=(-1)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=(-2)\\cdot 5-(-3)\\cdot (3)=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262823 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8c473f5-ef95-5227-a968-e2e86ab24e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463640} {:answer/id #uuid "ef280a56-6aa4-5367-afd4-c488c98b4baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef280a56-6aa4-5367-afd4-c488c98b4baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463641} :answer-field/id #uuid "bce7c6c8-b9b1-552a-b5e1-0f6140ff2c88" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464754} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "929235db-049d-563d-9c46-3e63d1f2cabc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463642} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9297a7-d7f3-5f84-9db4-8e4456568e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "929235db-049d-563d-9c46-3e63d1f2cabc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463642} :answer-field/id #uuid "48fb156a-09ce-5fde-8695-5588211123e1" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464755} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb27b827-2491-5ec9-8772-7e647962fd24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463644} {:answer/id #uuid "da00eb55-ba67-5112-89f2-1681a8d1c68d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da00eb55-ba67-5112-89f2-1681a8d1c68d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463645} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcd2d553-3e6c-5d1d-9ac4-1a5aba1b575d" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e8059f3-ef63-587d-911b-0d0c0a784873" :question/math-academy-id "q-127755" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f57cf2ee-5c54-5728-9819-04ba25ccaed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463646} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe95562-995d-540a-a75b-c6729affad85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f57cf2ee-5c54-5728-9819-04ba25ccaed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463646} :answer-field/id #uuid "09b46ce7-eeb0-59a8-90f1-679f8c0295ff" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bde6b23b-b56d-5b3d-a341-8a7675217e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463648} {:answer/id #uuid "306399cf-a4fb-5e1f-9e1c-fab262184a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "306399cf-a4fb-5e1f-9e1c-fab262184a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463649} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b22761-b532-55a6-93c3-281e6baeea2e" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464758} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad303f4b-49e7-5eb1-b038-2436daaa6d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463650} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3babfc-5f8a-55a0-949b-758d8eacf432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad303f4b-49e7-5eb1-b038-2436daaa6d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463650} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7b1f0e4-c9c9-5321-988b-aaf8e81cba4d" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "87b20497-ceac-5d64-8634-616821707ef5" :question/math-academy-id "q-127757" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nS=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $S$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(S)=1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(S)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $S$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot (-3)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)=0,$ we conclude that $T$ is not invertible. Since $T$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $T$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1)=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $T$ is singular."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d30b47ef-87b0-5e27-a184-0a096fd33124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463652} {:answer/id #uuid "33d939ee-6d35-51bf-8bb9-1d48cd53e796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33d939ee-6d35-51