ed\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A geometric distribution is used to model the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I follows a geometric distribution. Reviewing a file is a binomial experiment, and the number of files reviewed before the first infected file is found can be interpreted as the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.\n\n- Random variable II does *not* follow a geometric distribution. Finding an infected file is a binomial experiment, but the number of infected files in a computer cannot be interpreted as the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.\n\n- Random variable III follows a geometric distribution. Randomly picking out a crayon is a binomial experiment, and the number of crayons picked out before a blue crayon is picked can be interpreted as the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265919 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157314 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "06c1ce9a-bad7-50d6-b6c7-a1423ccce4bb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Geometric Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11b065d6-2fc9-5b93-bbcd-c8b5264efd65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463868} {:answer/id #uuid "8873e909-ba08-52af-be91-b6cac8bef178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11b065d6-2fc9-5b93-bbcd-c8b5264efd65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463868} :answer-field/id #uuid "debb