hich of the following random variables follow a geometric distribution?\n- **I.** The number of people examined at a clinic during a day\n- **II.** The average age of the people infected with a virus in a certain city\n- **III.** The number of people examined at a clinic until a person infected with a certain virus is found\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A geometric distribution is used to model the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I does *not* follow a geometric distribution. Being examined is a binomial experiment, but the number of people examined cannot be interpreted as the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.\n\n- Random variable II does *not* follow a geometric distribution. The average age of the people infected with a virus in a certain city is not a binomial experiment.\n\n- Random variable III follows a geometric distribution. Being examined is a binomial experiment, and the number of people examined until a person infected with a certain virus is found can be interpreted as the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a926134-0870-5528-985d-2c92e71158f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86d0fa0c-d83e-5302-8b19-931a556d2598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463874} {:answer/id #uuid "5f240d2f-1e1c-5d49-baec-e89948422632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f240d2f-1e1c-5d49-b